blem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} \\int_{0}^{\\sin{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}} 2 r\\,\\mathrm d r\\,\\mathrm d \\theta.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we integrate with respect to $r,$ treating $\\theta $ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} \\int_{0}^{\\sin{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}} 2 r\\,\\mathrm d r\\,\\mathrm d \\theta & = \\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} 2 \\int_{0}^{\\sin{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}} r\\,\\mathrm d r\\,\\mathrm d \\theta \\\\\n& = \\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} 2 \\left[\\frac{r^{2}}{2}\\right]_{0}^{\\sin{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}}\\,\\mathrm d \\theta \\\\\n& = \\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} 2 \\left(\\frac{\\left(\\sin{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\right)^{2}-\\left(0\\right)^{2}}{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm d \\theta \\\\\n& = \\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} \\sin^{2}{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm d \\theta\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the double-angle formula\n\n$$\n\\cos(2x)=1-2\\sin^2 x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=2\\theta$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\sin^2\\left(2\\theta\\right)=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(1-\\cos\\left(4\\theta\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nFinally, we can finish our integral by integrating with respect to $\\theta,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} \\sin^{2}{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm d \\theta & = \\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} \\frac{1}{2}\\left(1-\\cos\\left(4\\theta\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm d \\theta \\\\\n& = \\frac{1}{2}\\left[\\theta - \\frac{\\sin{\\left(4 \\theta \\right)}}{4}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} \\\\\n& = \\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}-\\frac{1}{4}\\sin\\left(\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}\\right)\\right)-\\left(0-\\frac{1}{4}\\sin\\left(0\\right)\\right)\\right) \\\\\n& = \\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}-\\frac{1}{4} \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)\\right)-\\left(0-\\frac{1}{4} \\left(0\\right)\\right)\\right) \\\\\n& = \\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)-\\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)\\right) \\\\\n& = - \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{16} + \\frac{\\pi}{12}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561304 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31881f34-a432-59b0-8b38-3684f13c3b52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\sqrt{3}}{4} + \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561274} {:answer/id #uuid "422e23d8-7878-5ea2-9a27-766bea4c942a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\sqrt{3}}{8} + \\frac{\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561278} {:answer/id #uuid "4d95f346-a420-5191-8ec2-3e7926314a93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\sqrt{3}}{16} + \\frac{\\pi}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561282} {:answer/id #uuid "f673e57e-d0b6-5998-93a3-565e128e73e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561305} {:answer/id #uuid "fe398fb7-a1e5-5acd-a33a-c5efe140276d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{\\pi}{2} - \\frac{3 \\sqrt{3}}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561307}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "422e23d8-7878-5ea2-9a27-766bea4c942a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\sqrt{3}}{8} + \\frac{\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561278} :answer-field/id #uuid "45be7b21-96cb-50e1-a316-7060f7c9bd71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561279}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "eacc9511-7fa5-53af-97be-32d0cbc36aff" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} \\int_{0}^{2 \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}} 3 r\\,\\mathrm d r\\,\\mathrm d \\theta.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we integrate with respect to $r,$ treating $\\theta $ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} \\int_{0}^{2 \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}} 3 r\\,\\mathrm d r\\,\\mathrm d \\theta & = \\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} 3 \\int_{0}^{2 \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}} r\\,\\mathrm d r\\,\\mathrm d \\theta \\\\\n& = \\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} 3 \\left[\\frac{r^{2}}{2}\\right]_{0}^{2 \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}}\\,\\mathrm d \\theta \\\\\n& = \\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} 3 \\left(\\frac{\\left(2 \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\right)^{2}-\\left(0\\right)^{2}}{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm d \\theta \\\\\n& = \\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} 6 \\cos^{2}{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm d \\theta\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the double-angle formula\n\n$$\n\\cos(2x)=2\\cos^2 x-1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=2\\theta$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\cos^2\\left(2\\theta\\right)=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(1+\\cos\\left(4\\theta\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nFinally, we can finish our integral by integrating with respect to $\\theta,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} 6 \\cos^{2}{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm d \\theta & = \\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} 3\\left(1+\\cos\\left(4\\theta\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm d \\theta \\\\\n& = 3\\left[\\theta + \\frac{\\sin{\\left(4 \\theta \\right)}}{4}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}} \\\\\n& = 3\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}+\\frac{1}{4}\\sin\\left(\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}\\right)\\right)-\\left(0+\\frac{1}{4}\\sin\\left(0\\right)\\right)\\right) \\\\\n& = 3\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}+\\frac{1}{4} \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)\\right)-\\left(0+\\frac{1}{4} \\left(0\\right)\\right)\\right) \\\\\n& = 3\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)+\\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)\\right) \\\\\n& = \\frac{3 \\sqrt{3}}{8} + \\frac{\\pi}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561317 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20f072ba-3739-59c5-8fe5-2f46c587a6d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 (t - 1) ((t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2} + (t - 3) (t - 1)^{3} + 1) e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561322} {:answer/id #uuid "41b0fbc7-8241-50ca-a1fc-d7076693e183" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(t - 1)^{4} (2 t - 6) e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561333} {:answer/id #uuid "5feae69f-7c55-5950-b155-315e04edd13d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2 t - 2) ((t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2} e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}} + e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561343} {:answer/id #uuid "aa16c309-d04e-5cf3-a65a-db91906040c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (t - 1)^{4} (2 t - 6) e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}} + (2 t - 2) ((t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2} e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}} + e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561359} {:answer/id #uuid "fa5f5b0e-4b3f-59bf-9b46-043cd0723f33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 (t - 1) ((t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2} + (t - 3) (t - 1)^{3} + 1) e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561380}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20f072ba-3739-59c5-8fe5-2f46c587a6d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 (t - 1) ((t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2} + (t - 3) (t - 1)^{3} + 1) e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561322} :answer-field/id #uuid "e738eb49-c04b-5d64-84fd-1070608d69a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561376}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "16bb4028-8696-5e87-8e7c-7e1a33c5c4cc" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=x e^{x y},$ $x=(t - 1)^{2}$ and $y=(t - 3)^{2},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}$." :question/worked-solution "![](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=x y e^{x y} + e^{x y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x^{2} e^{x y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2} e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}} + e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =(t - 1)^{4} e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} &=2 t - 2,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=2 t - 6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =((t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2} e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}} + e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}})\\cdot (2 t - 2)+((t - 1)^{4} e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}})\\cdot (2 t - 6) \\\\  & =(2 t - 2) e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}} + ((t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2} (2 t - 2) e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}}) + ((t - 1)^{4} (2 t - 6) e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}}) \\\\  & =2 (t - 1) ((t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2} + (t - 3) (t - 1)^{3} + 1) e^{(t - 3)^{2} (t - 1)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561328 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41376f0b-fddb-515b-9135-0dcfd4896483" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 27 t^{10} e^{3 t^{7}} + 12 t^{3} (3 t^{7} e^{3 t^{7}} + e^{3 t^{7}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561332} {:answer/id #uuid "6df73b83-3780-5113-98c9-ae7f6c812078" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12 t^{3} (3 t^{7} e^{3 t^{7}} + e^{3 t^{7}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561346} {:answer/id #uuid "809bb840-826d-5090-ab24-5ba97394b73e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27 t^{10} e^{3 t^{7}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561353} {:answer/id #uuid "811d9993-cbf5-58f2-82af-df6589b0f550" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 t^{3} (21 t^{7} + 4) e^{3 t^{7}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561354} {:answer/id #uuid "e92b5772-4089-5199-9617-602bbe124f77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 t^{3} (21 t^{7} + 4) e^{3 t^{7}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561379}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "811d9993-cbf5-58f2-82af-df6589b0f550" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 t^{3} (21 t^{7} + 4) e^{3 t^{7}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561354} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a990c52-96e6-5a56-8e2a-37b3d1997675" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561319}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "379f3d57-a4e8-5653-a290-2e107a7dab3c" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=x e^{x y},$ $x=3 t^{4}$ and $y=t^{3},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}$." :question/worked-solution "![](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=x y e^{x y} + e^{x y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x^{2} e^{x y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =3 t^{7} e^{3 t^{7}} + e^{3 t^{7}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =9 t^{8} e^{3 t^{7}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} &=12 t^{3},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=3 t^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =(3 t^{7} e^{3 t^{7}} + e^{3 t^{7}})\\cdot (12 t^{3})+(9 t^{8} e^{3 t^{7}})\\cdot (3 t^{2}) \\\\  & =12 t^{3} e^{3 t^{7}} + (36 t^{10} e^{3 t^{7}}) + (27 t^{10} e^{3 t^{7}}) \\\\  & =3 t^{3} (21 t^{7} + 4) e^{3 t^{7}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561337 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1849c99c-ec5f-564e-bd00-2693ebbb1567" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- t^{2} (5 t^{5} + 3) e^{t^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561318} {:answer/id #uuid "212f23b1-5655-5afe-ac3f-c0a1b51cbabf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 t^{7} e^{t^{5}} + 3 t^{2} (t^{5} e^{t^{5}} + e^{t^{5}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561323} {:answer/id #uuid "4b78b10d-4899-5250-a89d-b0ffe4794c07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 t^{7} e^{t^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561339} {:answer/id #uuid "77c6e33f-6d12-5c5d-b983-ae5efd0acca4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t^{2} (5 t^{5} + 3) e^{t^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561351} {:answer/id #uuid "9928a079-eba2-5e28-93d4-777658d1302b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 t^{2} (t^{5} e^{t^{5}} + e^{t^{5}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561358}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77c6e33f-6d12-5c5d-b983-ae5efd0acca4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t^{2} (5 t^{5} + 3) e^{t^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561351} :answer-field/id #uuid "03c9cabd-fbbb-5023-88c9-3c2c7ba49282" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561312}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4946f9ea-a5fa-50ee-8aec-931b80816d77" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=x e^{x y},$ $x=t^{3}$ and $y=t^{2},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}$." :question/worked-solution "![](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=x y e^{x y} + e^{x y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x^{2} e^{x y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =t^{5} e^{t^{5}} + e^{t^{5}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =t^{6} e^{t^{5}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} &=3 t^{2},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=2 t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =(t^{5} e^{t^{5}} + e^{t^{5}})\\cdot (3 t^{2})+(t^{6} e^{t^{5}})\\cdot (2 t) \\\\  & =3 t^{2} e^{t^{5}} + (3 t^{7} e^{t^{5}}) + (2 t^{7} e^{t^{5}}) \\\\  & =t^{2} (5 t^{5} + 3) e^{t^{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561348 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c83790c-a703-5058-8cbf-04d4152546fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (3 t + 2)^{4} (18 t + 12) e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}} + (18 t + 12) ((3 t + 2)^{4} e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}} + e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561320} {:answer/id #uuid "4509ef26-9cd8-5023-a2e9-3e0842651cf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(18 t + 12) ((3 t + 2)^{4} e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}} + e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561336} {:answer/id #uuid "9218d13e-7ce3-5386-9247-59aab07237b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 (3 t + 2) (2 (3 t + 2)^{4} + 1) e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561356} {:answer/id #uuid "b67e6ad5-a679-54e7-8ac2-2efd98b370e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3 t + 2)^{4} (18 t + 12) e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561362} {:answer/id #uuid "ddfe92d1-9dd2-5418-af08-95dd922c1931" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 (3 t + 2) (2 (3 t + 2)^{4} + 1) e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561372}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ddfe92d1-9dd2-5418-af08-95dd922c1931" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 (3 t + 2) (2 (3 t + 2)^{4} + 1) e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561372} :answer-field/id #uuid "30d27a3a-17ea-543d-b1a0-88e5b60881b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561327}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6ff56f6d-0609-54ae-950b-f994f207b14c" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=x e^{x y},$ $x=(3 t + 2)^{2}$ and $y=(3 t + 2)^{2},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}$." :question/worked-solution "![](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=x y e^{x y} + e^{x y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x^{2} e^{x y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =(3 t + 2)^{4} e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}} + e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =(3 t + 2)^{4} e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} &=18 t + 12,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=18 t + 12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =((3 t + 2)^{4} e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}} + e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}})\\cdot (18 t + 12)+((3 t + 2)^{4} e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}})\\cdot (18 t + 12) \\\\  & =(18 t + 12) e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}} + ((3 t + 2)^{4} (18 t + 12) e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}}) + ((3 t + 2)^{4} (18 t + 12) e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}}) \\\\  & =6 (3 t + 2) (2 (3 t + 2)^{4} + 1) e^{(3 t + 2)^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561352 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0753e31c-5005-5a9b-a87b-f91a8c8a77a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 t (2 t^{5} e^{2 t^{5}} + e^{2 t^{5}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561313} {:answer/id #uuid "447c7f99-fdb6-5457-8d9a-e3aa9f50861f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12 t^{6} e^{2 t^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561335} {:answer/id #uuid "60fde45f-357e-58f4-affa-c5ef9a2b31ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 12 t^{6} e^{2 t^{5}} + 4 t (2 t^{5} e^{2 t^{5}} + e^{2 t^{5}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561344} {:answer/id #uuid "d5960284-1fb4-5fe6-a6cc-93c721a5098b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 t (5 t^{5} + 1) e^{2 t^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561371} {:answer/id #uuid "e8702b54-5e62-56c8-9256-f605b63609ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 t (5 t^{5} + 1) e^{2 t^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561378}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8702b54-5e62-56c8-9256-f605b63609ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 t (5 t^{5} + 1) e^{2 t^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561378} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3d976a4-de41-5ed3-b5d4-88d3dc494011" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561375}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "77e86c5a-4b57-5eb8-8644-abcaf34b69bc" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=x e^{x y},$ $x=2 t^{2}$ and $y=t^{3},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}$." :question/worked-solution "![](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=x y e^{x y} + e^{x y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x^{2} e^{x y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =2 t^{5} e^{2 t^{5}} + e^{2 t^{5}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =4 t^{4} e^{2 t^{5}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} &=4 t,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=3 t^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =(2 t^{5} e^{2 t^{5}} + e^{2 t^{5}})\\cdot (4 t)+(4 t^{4} e^{2 t^{5}})\\cdot (3 t^{2}) \\\\  & =4 t e^{2 t^{5}} + (8 t^{6} e^{2 t^{5}}) + (12 t^{6} e^{2 t^{5}}) \\\\  & =4 t (5 t^{5} + 1) e^{2 t^{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561355 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12df19e5-92b7-5d33-8757-cda8739d3e6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 (3 t + 2) ((3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2} + (3 t - 2) (3 t + 2)^{3} + 1) e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561315} {:answer/id #uuid "545d27d9-3cfd-5eeb-aea7-0eab883c4b69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (3 t + 2)^{4} (18 t - 12) e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}} + (18 t + 12) ((3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2} e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}} + e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561340} {:answer/id #uuid "5b75c05a-d660-5abe-a52d-9ab9e3a38c8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 (3 t + 2) ((3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2} + (3 t - 2) (3 t + 2)^{3} + 1) e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561342} {:answer/id #uuid "aba30610-805a-5061-a2ce-fde43245da17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3 t + 2)^{4} (18 t - 12) e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561360} {:answer/id #uuid "bf49f816-92b6-5bc8-a43f-a220f9f453a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(18 t + 12) ((3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2} e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}} + e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561365}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12df19e5-92b7-5d33-8757-cda8739d3e6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 (3 t + 2) ((3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2} + (3 t - 2) (3 t + 2)^{3} + 1) e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561315} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1775f0e-8e1b-5b4b-9760-0645558c6cf5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561367}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8d01c121-a85c-5572-ac96-07c83af29d68" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=x e^{x y},$ $x=(3 t + 2)^{2}$ and $y=(3 t - 2)^{2},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}$." :question/worked-solution "![](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=x y e^{x y} + e^{x y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x^{2} e^{x y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2} e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}} + e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =(3 t + 2)^{4} e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} &=18 t + 12,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=18 t - 12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =((3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2} e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}} + e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}})\\cdot (18 t + 12)+((3 t + 2)^{4} e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}})\\cdot (18 t - 12) \\\\  & =(18 t + 12) e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}} + ((3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2} (18 t + 12) e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}}) + ((3 t + 2)^{4} (18 t - 12) e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}}) \\\\  & =6 (3 t + 2) ((3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2} + (3 t - 2) (3 t + 2)^{3} + 1) e^{(3 t - 2)^{2} (3 t + 2)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561364 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e1c7a8e-0422-5233-b088-e2341346c984" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 8 t (12 t^{6} + 1) e^{4 t^{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561321} {:answer/id #uuid "5b61d18a-70d2-5b67-a497-85ceecaad618" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 t (4 t^{6} e^{4 t^{6}} + e^{4 t^{6}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561341} {:answer/id #uuid "6f1b3dcf-deeb-5278-88c3-40be3d31308c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64 t^{7} e^{4 t^{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561347} {:answer/id #uuid "774a3c97-56bd-5fbe-bf9f-4aa50c321d1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 t (12 t^{6} + 1) e^{4 t^{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561350} {:answer/id #uuid "e024a943-4b21-5e6c-99ff-b264cf508bf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 64 t^{7} e^{4 t^{6}} + 8 t (4 t^{6} e^{4 t^{6}} + e^{4 t^{6}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561374}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "774a3c97-56bd-5fbe-bf9f-4aa50c321d1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 t (12 t^{6} + 1) e^{4 t^{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561350} :answer-field/id #uuid "b48d05a5-03ed-527d-b03e-d22708b9e3bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561361}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ba6447ed-c55a-5176-ab21-a18af111a0e0" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=x e^{x y},$ $x=4 t^{2}$ and $y=t^{4},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}$." :question/worked-solution "![](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=x y e^{x y} + e^{x y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x^{2} e^{x y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =4 t^{6} e^{4 t^{6}} + e^{4 t^{6}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =16 t^{4} e^{4 t^{6}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} &=8 t,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=4 t^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =(4 t^{6} e^{4 t^{6}} + e^{4 t^{6}})\\cdot (8 t)+(16 t^{4} e^{4 t^{6}})\\cdot (4 t^{3}) \\\\  & =8 t e^{4 t^{6}} + (32 t^{7} e^{4 t^{6}}) + (64 t^{7} e^{4 t^{6}}) \\\\  & =8 t (12 t^{6} + 1) e^{4 t^{6}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
